 "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/state.json" "file_sha256" "08c5c3665d17667bbd39e9081097191f4f06272b1997c6e28213a4e9b1baf7b9"} {"question" "q-320045" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "9"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/state.json" "file_sha256" "08c5c3665d17667bbd39e9081097191f4f06272b1997c6e28213a4e9b1baf7b9"} {"question" "q-125885" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $0W$, if \n$W=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/state.json" "file_sha256" "08c5c3665d17667bbd39e9081097191f4f06272b1997c6e28213a4e9b1baf7b9"} {"question" "q-125885" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We multiply each entry of $W$ by $0,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0W & =0[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0\\cdot 1 & 0\\cdot (-1) & 0\\cdot (-3) \\\\ 0\\cdot (-5) & 0\\cdot 0 & 0\\cdot 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/state.json" "file_sha256" "08c5c3665d17667bbd39e9081097191f4f06272b1997c6e28213a4e9b1baf7b9"} {"question" "q-125885" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "077ee17b6c9bc23c235d295819c1889caf468bb4e02214c764226c5c342260fc"} {"question" "q-125885" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/state.json" "file_sha256" "08c5c3665d17667bbd39e9081097191f4f06272b1997c6e28213a4e9b1baf7b9"} {"question" "q-125885" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/state.json" "file_sha256" "08c5c3665d17667bbd39e9081097191f4f06272b1997c6e28213a4e9b1baf7b9"} {"question" "q-125885" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/state.json" "file_sha256" "08c5c3665d17667bbd39e9081097191f4f06272b1997c6e28213a4e9b1baf7b9"} {"question" "q-320563" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $kB=[\\begin{aligned}8 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}]$,\nwhere $B=[\\begin{aligned}24 & -12 & 6\\end{aligned}]$\nand $k$ is a scalar, calculate the value of $k.$\n\n$k=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/state.json" "file_sha256" "08c5c3665d17667bbd39e9081097191f4f06272b1997c6e28213a4e9b1baf7b9"} {"question" "q-320563" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To express $kB,$ we multiply each entry of $B$ by $k,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}kB & =k[\\begin{aligned}24 & -12 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}24k & -12k & 6k\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the above result equal to the matrix given for $kB$ in the problem statement:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}24k & -12k & 6k\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}8 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWe can solve for $k$ by equating any two corresponding (nonzero) elements. Let's choose the rightmost elements, $6k$ and $2.$ Equating these elements, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6k & =2 \\\\ k & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Note:** We would still get the same result if we chose any other two corresponding (nonzero) elements." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/state.json" "file_sha256" "08c5c3665d17667bbd39e9081097191f4f06272b1997c6e28213a4e9b1baf7b9"} {"question" "q-320563" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "077ee17b6c9bc23c235d295819c1889caf468bb4e02214c764226c5c342260fc"} {"question" "q-320563" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/state.json" "file_sha256" "08c5c3665d17667bbd39e9081097191f4f06272b1997c6e28213a4e9b1baf7b9"} {"question" "q-320563" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/state.json" "file_sha256" "08c5c3665d17667bbd39e9081097191f4f06272b1997c6e28213a4e9b1baf7b9"} {"question" "q-69670" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $kS=[\\begin{aligned}63 & -28 \\\\ 0 & -56\\end{aligned}]$,\nwhere $S=[\\begin{aligned}-9 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 8\\end{aligned}]$\nand $k$ is a scalar, calculate the value of $k.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/state.json" "file_sha256" "08c5c3665d17667bbd39e9081097191f4f06272b1997c6e28213a4e9b1baf7b9"} {"question" "q-69670" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To express $kS,$ we multiply each entry of $S$ by $k,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}kS & =k[\\begin{aligned}-9 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-9k & 4k \\\\ 0 & 8k\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the above result equal to the matrix given for $kS$ in the problem statement:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-9k & 4k \\\\ 0 & 8k\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}63 & -28 \\\\ 0 & -56\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWe can solve for $k$ by equating any two corresponding (nonzero) elements. Let's choose the top-left elements, $-9k$ and $63.$ Equating these elements, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-9k & =63 \\\\ k & =-7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Note:** We would still get the same result if we chose any other two corresponding (nonzero) elements." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/state.json" "file_sha256" "08c5c3665d17667bbd39e9081097191f4f06272b1997c6e28213a4e9b1baf7b9"} {"question" "q-69670" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "077ee17b6c9bc23c235d295819c1889caf468bb4e02214c764226c5c342260fc"} {"question" "q-69670" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/state.json" "file_sha256" "08c5c3665d17667bbd39e9081097191f4f06272b1997c6e28213a4e9b1baf7b9"} {"question" "q-69670" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "k=-2"] ["math" "k=-3"] ["math" "k=-6"] ["math" "k=-7"] ["math" "k=0"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/state.json" "file_sha256" "08c5c3665d17667bbd39e9081097191f4f06272b1997c6e28213a4e9b1baf7b9"} {"question" "q-69670" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "k=-7"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/state.json" "file_sha256" "08c5c3665d17667bbd39e9081097191f4f06272b1997c6e28213a4e9b1baf7b9"} {"question" "q-320536" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $kB=[\\begin{aligned}33 & 36 \\\\ -12 & -24\\end{aligned}]$,\nwhere $B=[\\begin{aligned}11 & 12 \\\\ -4 & -8\\end{aligned}]$\nand $k$ is a scalar, calculate the value of $k.$\n\n$k=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/state.json" "file_sha256" "08c5c3665d17667bbd39e9081097191f4f06272b1997c6e28213a4e9b1baf7b9"} {"question" "q-320536" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To express $kB,$ we multiply each entry of $B$ by $k,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}kB & =k[\\begin{aligned}11 & 12 \\\\ 4 & -8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}11k & 12k \\\\ 4k & -8k\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the above result equal to the matrix given for $kB$ in the problem statement:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}11k & 12k \\\\ -4k & -8k\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}33 & 36 \\\\ -12 & -24\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWe can solve for $k$ by equating any two corresponding (nonzero) elements. Let's choose the bottom-left elements, $-4k$ and $-12.$ Equating these elements, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4k & =-12 \\\\ k & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Note:** We would still get the same result if we chose any other two corresponding (nonzero) elements." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/state.json" "file_sha256" "08c5c3665d17667bbd39e9081097191f4f06272b1997c6e28213a4e9b1baf7b9"} {"question" "q-320536" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "077ee17b6c9bc23c235d295819c1889caf468bb4e02214c764226c5c342260fc"} {"question" "q-320536" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/state.json" "file_sha256" "08c5c3665d17667bbd39e9081097191f4f06272b1997c6e28213a4e9b1baf7b9"} {"question" "q-320536" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/state.json" "file_sha256" "08c5c3665d17667bbd39e9081097191f4f06272b1997c6e28213a4e9b1baf7b9"} {"question" "q-320551" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $kW=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 20 & -15 \\\\ 10 & -10 & 25\\end{aligned}]$,\nwhere $W=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 5\\end{aligned}]$\nand $k$ is a scalar, calculate the value of $k.$\n\n$k=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/state.json" "file_sha256" "08c5c3665d17667bbd39e9081097191f4f06272b1997c6e28213a4e9b1baf7b9"} {"question" "q-320551" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To express $kW,$ we multiply each entry of $W$ by $k,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}kW & =k[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}k & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4k & -3k \\\\ 2k & -2k & 5k\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the above result equal to the matrix given for $kW$ in the problem statement:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}k & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4k & -3k \\\\ 2k & -2k & 5k\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 20 & -15 \\\\ 10 & -10 & 25\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWe can solve for $k$ by equating any two corresponding (nonzero) elements. Let's choose the  leftmost elements of the third row, $2k$ and $10.$ Equating these elements, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2k & =10 \\\\ k & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Note:** We would still get the same result if we chose any other two corresponding (nonzero) elements." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/state.json" "file_sha256" "08c5c3665d17667bbd39e9081097191f4f06272b1997c6e28213a4e9b1baf7b9"} {"question" "q-320551" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "077ee17b6c9bc23c235d295819c1889caf468bb4e02214c764226c5c342260fc"} {"question" "q-320551" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/state.json" "file_sha256" "08c5c3665d17667bbd39e9081097191f4f06272b1997c6e28213a4e9b1baf7b9"} {"question" "q-320551" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/state.json" "file_sha256" "08c5c3665d17667bbd39e9081097191f4f06272b1997c6e28213a4e9b1baf7b9"} {"question" "q-981" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $kA=[\\begin{aligned}-7 & -21 & 56\\end{aligned}]$,\nwhere $A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 & 8\\end{aligned}]$\nand $k$ is a scalar, calculate the value of $k.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/state.json" "file_sha256" "08c5c3665d17667bbd39e9081097191f4f06272b1997c6e28213a4e9b1baf7b9"} {"question" "q-981" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To express $kA,$ we multiply each entry of $A$ by $k,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}kA & =k\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 & 8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-k & -3k & 8k\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the above result equal to the matrix given for $kA$ in the problem statement:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-k & -3k & 8k\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-7 & -21 & 56\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWe can solve for $k$ by equating any two corresponding (nonzero) elements. Let's choose the leftmost elements, $-k$ and $-7.$ Equating these elements, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-k & =-7 \\\\ k & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Note:** We would still get the same result if we chose any other two corresponding (nonzero) elements." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/state.json" "file_sha256" "08c5c3665d17667bbd39e9081097191f4f06272b1997c6e28213a4e9b1baf7b9"} {"question" "q-981" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "077ee17b6c9bc23c235d295819c1889caf468bb4e02214c764226c5c342260fc"} {"question" "q-981" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/state.json" "file_sha256" "08c5c3665d17667bbd39e9081097191f4f06272b1997c6e28213a4e9b1baf7b9"} {"question" "q-981" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "k=3"] ["math" "k=4"] ["math" "k=5"] ["math" "k=6"] ["math" "k=7"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/state.json" "file_sha256" "08c5c3665d17667bbd39e9081097191f4f06272b1997c6e28213a4e9b1baf7b9"} {"question" "q-981" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "k=7"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/state.json" "file_sha256" "08c5c3665d17667bbd39e9081097191f4f06272b1997c6e28213a4e9b1baf7b9"} {"question" "q-69642" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\frac{1}{3}G+2H$, where\n$G=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 6 & 15 \\\\ -12 & 9 & 6\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$H=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 6\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/state.json" "file_sha256" "08c5c3665d17667bbd39e9081097191f4f06272b1997c6e28213a4e9b1baf7b9"} {"question" "q-69642" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We multiply each entry of $G$ by $\\frac{1}{3}$ and each entry of $H$ by $2,$ and then add the resulting matrices, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}G+2H & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 6 & 15 \\\\ -12 & 9 & 6\\end{aligned}]+2[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 3 & \\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 6 & \\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 15 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\cdot (-12) & \\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 9 & \\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 6\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2\\cdot 1 & 2\\cdot 2 & 2\\cdot 5 \\\\ 2\\cdot 3 & 2\\cdot 4 & 2\\cdot 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ -4 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & 10 \\\\ 6 & 8 & 12\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1+2 & 2+4 & 5+10 \\\\ -4+6 & 3+8 & 2+12\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 6 & 15 \\\\ 2 & 11 & 14\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/state.json" "file_sha256" "08c5c3665d17667bbd39e9081097191f4f06272b1997c6e28213a4e9b1baf7b9"} {"question" "q-69642" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "077ee17b6c9bc23c235d295819c1889caf468bb4e02214c764226c5c342260fc"} {"question" "q-69642" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/state.json" "file_sha256" "08c5c3665d17667bbd39e9081097191f4f06272b1997c6e28213a4e9b1baf7b9"} {"question" "q-69642" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & 15 \\\\ -2 & 11 & 14\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 15 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 14 & 11\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 11 & 10\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 6 & 14 \\\\ 2 & 11 & 15\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 6 & 15 \\\\ 2 & 11 & 14\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/state.json" "file_sha256" "08c5c3665d17667bbd39e9081097191f4f06272b1997c6e28213a4e9b1baf7b9"} {"question" "q-69642" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 6 & 15 \\\\ 2 & 11 & 14\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/state.json" "file_sha256" "08c5c3665d17667bbd39e9081097191f4f06272b1997c6e28213a4e9b1baf7b9"} {"question" "q-126009" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $-A+2B$, where\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$B=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/state.json" "file_sha256" "08c5c3665d17667bbd39e9081097191f4f06272b1997c6e28213a4e9b1baf7b9"} {"question" "q-126009" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We multiply each entry of $A$ by $-1$ and each entry of $B$ by $2,$ and then add the resulting matrices, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-A+2B & =(-1)[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]+2[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}(-1)\\cdot 3 & (-1)\\cdot 1 \\\\ (-1)\\cdot 1 & (-1)\\cdot 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2\\cdot 0 & 2\\cdot (-2) \\\\ 2\\cdot (-2) & 2\\cdot 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3+0 & -1+(-4) \\\\ -1+(-4) & 0+4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -5 \\\\ -5 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/state.json" "file_sha256" "08c5c3665d17667bbd39e9081097191f4f06272b1997c6e28213a4e9b1baf7b9"} {"question" "q-126009" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "077ee17b6c9bc23c235d295819c1889caf468bb4e02214c764226c5c342260fc"} {"question" "q-126009" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/state.json" "file_sha256" "08c5c3665d17667bbd39e9081097191f4f06272b1997c6e28213a4e9b1baf7b9"} {"question" "q-126009" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -5 \\\\ -5 & 4\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}2 & -5 \\\\ -4 & 4\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/state.json" "file_sha256" "08c5c3665d17667bbd39e9081097191f4f06272b1997c6e28213a4e9b1baf7b9"} {"question" "q-126009" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -5 \\\\ -5 & 4\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/state.json" "file_sha256" "08c5c3665d17667bbd39e9081097191f4f06272b1997c6e28213a4e9b1baf7b9"} {"question" "q-320656" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $4F-\\frac{1}{2}G$, where\n$F=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$G=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 4 & -6\\end{aligned}].$\n\n| $4F-\\frac{1}{2}G=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/state.json" "file_sha256" "08c5c3665d17667bbd39e9081097191f4f06272b1997c6e28213a4e9b1baf7b9"} {"question" "q-320656" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We multiply each entry of $F$ by $4$ and each entry of $G$ by $\\frac{1}{2},$ and then subtract the resulting matrices, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4F-\\frac{1}{2}G & =4[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 4 & -6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4\\cdot 4 & 4\\cdot (-1) & 4\\cdot 0 & 4\\cdot 2\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2 & \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4 & \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-6)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}16 & -4 & 0 & 8\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}16-1 & -4-0 & 0-2 & 8-(-3)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}15 & -4 & -2 & 11\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/state.json" "file_sha256" "08c5c3665d17667bbd39e9081097191f4f06272b1997c6e28213a4e9b1baf7b9"} {"question" "q-320656" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "077ee17b6c9bc23c235d295819c1889caf468bb4e02214c764226c5c342260fc"} {"question" "q-320656" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/state.json" "file_sha256" "08c5c3665d17667bbd39e9081097191f4f06272b1997c6e28213a4e9b1baf7b9"} {"question" "q-320656" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "15"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/state.json" "file_sha256" "08c5c3665d17667bbd39e9081097191f4f06272b1997c6e28213a4e9b1baf7b9"} {"question" "q-320656" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/state.json" "file_sha256" "08c5c3665d17667bbd39e9081097191f4f06272b1997c6e28213a4e9b1baf7b9"} {"question" "q