| {{field-4}} |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/state.json" "file_sha256" "08c5c3665d17667bbd39e9081097191f4f06272b1997c6e28213a4e9b1baf7b9"} {"question" "q-320671" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We multiply each entry of $M$ by $\\frac{2}{3}$ and each entry of $N$ by $2,$ and then add the resulting matrices, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3}M+2N & =\\frac{2}{3}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 & 15 \\\\ -12 & 6 & 0\\end{aligned}]+2[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & \\frac{1}{2} & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot 6 & \\frac{2}{3}\\cdot 0 & \\frac{2}{3}\\cdot 15 \\\\ \\frac{2}{3}\\cdot (-12) & \\frac{2}{3}\\cdot 6 & \\frac{2}{3}\\cdot 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2\\cdot 3 & 2\\cdot (-1) & 2\\cdot 0 \\\\ 2\\cdot (-2) & 2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} & 2\\cdot (-1)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 10 \\\\ -8 & 4 & 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}6 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4+6 & 0-2 & 10+0 \\\\ -8-4 & 4+1 & 0-2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}10 & -2 & 10 \\\\ -12 & 5 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/state.json" "file_sha256" "08c5c3665d17667bbd39e9081097191f4f06272b1997c6e28213a4e9b1baf7b9"} {"question" "q-320671" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "077ee17b6c9bc23c235d295819c1889caf468bb4e02214c764226c5c342260fc"} {"question" "q-320671" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/state.json" "file_sha256" "08c5c3665d17667bbd39e9081097191f4f06272b1997c6e28213a4e9b1baf7b9"} {"question" "q-320671" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "10"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/state.json" "file_sha256" "08c5c3665d17667bbd39e9081097191f4f06272b1997c6e28213a4e9b1baf7b9"} {"question" "q-320671" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/state.json" "file_sha256" "08c5c3665d17667bbd39e9081097191f4f06272b1997c6e28213a4e9b1baf7b9"} {"question" "q-320671" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "10"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/state.json" "file_sha256" "08c5c3665d17667bbd39e9081097191f4f06272b1997c6e28213a4e9b1baf7b9"} {"question" "q-320671" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/state.json" "file_sha256" "08c5c3665d17667bbd39e9081097191f4f06272b1997c6e28213a4e9b1baf7b9"} {"question" "q-320671" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/state.json" "file_sha256" "08c5c3665d17667bbd39e9081097191f4f06272b1997c6e28213a4e9b1baf7b9"} {"question" "q-320671" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/state.json" "file_sha256" "08c5c3665d17667bbd39e9081097191f4f06272b1997c6e28213a4e9b1baf7b9"} {"question" "q-320671" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/state.json" "file_sha256" "08c5c3665d17667bbd39e9081097191f4f06272b1997c6e28213a4e9b1baf7b9"} {"question" "q-11531" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $3F+\\frac{1}{2}G$, where\n$F=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$G=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 6\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/state.json" "file_sha256" "08c5c3665d17667bbd39e9081097191f4f06272b1997c6e28213a4e9b1baf7b9"} {"question" "q-11531" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We multiply each entry of $F$ by $3$ and each entry of $G$ by $\\frac{1}{2},$ and then add the resulting matrices, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3F+\\frac{1}{2}G & =3[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]+\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3\\cdot 1 & 3\\cdot 3 \\\\ 3\\cdot (-2) & 3\\cdot 2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2 & \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4 & \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 9 \\\\ -6 & 6\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3+1 & 9+0 \\\\ -6+2 & 6+3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 9 \\\\ -4 & 9\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/state.json" "file_sha256" "08c5c3665d17667bbd39e9081097191f4f06272b1997c6e28213a4e9b1baf7b9"} {"question" "q-11531" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "077ee17b6c9bc23c235d295819c1889caf468bb4e02214c764226c5c342260fc"} {"question" "q-11531" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/state.json" "file_sha256" "08c5c3665d17667bbd39e9081097191f4f06272b1997c6e28213a4e9b1baf7b9"} {"question" "q-11531" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 9 \\\\ -4 & 9\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}4 & -9 \\\\ -4 & 9\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}4 & 9 \\\\ -4 & -9\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}4 & 9 \\\\ -4 & 9\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}4 & 9 \\\\ 9 & -4\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/state.json" "file_sha256" "08c5c3665d17667bbd39e9081097191f4f06272b1997c6e28213a4e9b1baf7b9"} {"question" "q-11531" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}4 & 9 \\\\ -4 & 9\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/state.json" "file_sha256" "08c5c3665d17667bbd39e9081097191f4f06272b1997c6e28213a4e9b1baf7b9"} {"question" "e-4380" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $-2A$, if \n$A=\\left\\lbrack\n    \t\\matrix {\n        \t2 & -1 \\\n        \t4 & 7\n    \t}\n    \t\\right\\rbrack.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/example-4380.json" "file_sha256" "db731f34b39207a5e9627a3e5fc406f0f0f8355fbcc5c043adba1c44edb49939"} {"question" "e-4380" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We multiply each entry of $A$ by $-2,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2A & =-2[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2\\cdot 2 & -2\\cdot (-1) \\\\ -2\\cdot 4 & -2\\cdot 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 2 \\\\ -8 & -14\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/example-4380.json" "file_sha256" "db731f34b39207a5e9627a3e5fc406f0f0f8355fbcc5c043adba1c44edb49939"} {"question" "e-4381" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $k {A} =\n\\left\\lbrack\n    \t\\matrix {\n        \t1 & 3 & 4 \\\n        \t6 & 0 & -2\n    \t}\n    \t\\right\\rbrack,$\nwhere ${A} =\n\\left\\lbrack\n    \t\\matrix {\n        \t2 & 6 & 8 \\\n        \t12 & 0 & -4\n    \t}\n    \t\\right\\rbrack$\nand $k$ is a scalar, calculate the value of $k.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/example-4381.json" "file_sha256" "ab732c9226d9a7fae5a75ed421174ee81bc125939c2a36aff17bcbe89a57c7a6"} {"question" "e-4381" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To express $kA,$ we multiply each entry of $A$ by $k,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}kA & =k\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & 6 & 8 \\\\ 12 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2k & 6k & 8k \\\\ 12k & 0 & -4k\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the above result equal to the matrix given for $kA$ in the problem statement:\n\n$$\n\\left\\lbrack\n    \t\\matrix {\n        \t2k & 6k & 8k \\\n        \t12k & 0 & -4k\n    \t}\n    \t\\right\\rbrack\n=\n\\left\\lbrack\n    \t\\matrix {\n        \t1 & 3 & 4 \\\n        \t6 & 0 & -2\n    \t}\n    \t\\right\\rbrack\n$$\n\nWe can solve for $k$ by equating any two corresponding (nonzero) elements. Let's choose the top-left elements, $2k$ and $1.$ Equating these elements, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2k & =1 \\\\ k & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Note:** We would still get the same result if we chose any other two corresponding (nonzero) elements." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/example-4381.json" "file_sha256" "ab732c9226d9a7fae5a75ed421174ee81bc125939c2a36aff17bcbe89a57c7a6"} {"question" "e-4382" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $2 {A} + \\dfrac{1}{2} {B}$, where\n$[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]$ and ${B}=\n    \\left\\lbrack\n    \\matrix {\n        0 & 2 \\\n        4 & 2\n    }\n    \\right\\rbrack\n.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/example-4382.json" "file_sha256" "9f25a7593bd311d46e618b58e62cf7684b669b198550c018f9be238db9e2312a"} {"question" "e-4382" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We multiply each entry of $A$ by $2$ and each entry of $B$ by $\\dfrac{1}{2},$ and then add the resulting matrices, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2A+\\frac{1}{2}B & =2[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]+\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\cdot 1 & 2\\cdot 5 \\\\ 2\\cdot 1 & 2\\cdot 2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4 & \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 10 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2+0 & 10+1 \\\\ 2+2 & 4+1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 11 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972893/example-4382.json" "file_sha256" "9f25a7593bd311d46e618b58e62cf7684b669b198550c018f9be238db9e2312a"}] "usage" {"e-4382" [] "e-4381" [] "q-981" [] "e-4380" []} "basis" 757 "retractions" [[17592186060380 :question/problem "If $kA = \\begin{bmatrix}-7 & -21 & 56\\end{bmatrix}$,\n\nwhere $A = \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -3 & 8\\end{bmatrix}$\nand $k$ is a scalar, calculate the value of $k$."] [17592186059473 :question/problem "Calculate $-2A$, if\n$A=\\left\\lbrack \\matrix {2 & -1 \\ 4 & 7} \\right\\rbrack$."] [17592186059473 :question/worked-solution "We multiply each entry of $A$ by $-2$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-2A &= -2\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\cdot 2 & -2 \\cdot (-1) \\\\ -2 \\cdot 4 & -2 \\cdot 7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 2 \\\\ -8 & -14\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186059474 :question/problem "If $k {A} = \\left\\lbrack \\matrix {1 & 3 & 4 \\ 6 & 0 & -2} \\right\\rbrack$,\nwhere ${A} = \\left\\lbrack \\matrix {2 & 6 & 8 \\ 12 & 0 & -4} \\right\\rbrack$\nand $k$ is a scalar, calculate the value of $k$."] [17592186059474 :question/worked-solution "To express $kA$, we multiply each entry of $A$ by $k$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nkA &= k \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 6 & 8 \\\\ 12 & 0 & -4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}2k & 6k & 8k \\\\ 12k & 0 & -4k\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the above result equal to the matrix given for $kA$ in the problem statement:\n\n$$\n\\left\\lbrack \\matrix {2k & 6k & 8k \\ 12k & 0 & -4k} \\right\\rbrack = \\left\\lbrack \\matrix {1 & 3 & 4 \\ 6 & 0 & -2} \\right\\rbrack\n$$\n\nWe can solve for $k$ by equating any two corresponding (nonzero) elements. Let's choose the top-left elements, $2k$ and $1$. Equating these elements, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2k &= 1 \\\\\nk &= \\frac{1}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Note:** We would still get the same result if we chose any other two corresponding (nonzero) elements."] [17592186059475 :question/problem "Calculate $2 {A} + \\dfrac{1}{2} {B}$, where\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$ and ${B}= \\left\\lbrack \\matrix {0 & 2 \\ 4 & 2} \\right\\rbrack$."] [17592186059475 :question/worked-solution "We multiply each entry of $A$ by $2$ and each entry of $B$ by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{2}\n$$\n\nand then add the resulting matrices, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2A + \\frac{1}{2}B &= 2\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} + \\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\cdot 1 & 2 \\cdot 5 \\\\ 2 \\cdot 1 & 2 \\cdot 2\\end{bmatrix} + \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 0 & \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 2 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 4 & \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 10 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix} + \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}2 + 0 & 10 + 1 \\\\ 2 + 2 & 4 + 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 11 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186059264 17592186059265 17592186059266 17592186059267 17592186059268] "immutable_fields" [[17592186059263 :answer-field/correct] [17592186059263 :answer-field/id] [17592186059263 :answer-field/key] [17592186059263 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
